Author: conlaw1 <con.lawless@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 6 20:33:25 2026 -0400

    feat: execution plan Phases 0-3 — messaging core, differentiators, trust dial
    
    Full change inventory in docs/implementation-log-2026-08-06.md; plan in
    docs/execution-plan-2026-08-06.md.
    
    Phase 0 — fixes
    - Run-of-show generator repaired: the system prompt demanded ISO
      timestamps with offsets while the Zod schema rejected them. A
      flexibleDatetime transform normalizes any parseable ISO form to UTC,
      plus a one-shot repair pass that feeds validation issues back to the
      model before failing.
    - No raw error dumps in the UI: servers emit short codes only and
      lib/ai/friendly-error.ts maps them to calm copy, collapsing anything
      unrecognized (JSON, stack fragments) to a generic line.
    - /studio/insights aliases to /studio/reports (was a 404); whole-row
      click targets on CRM tables; "Draft a run of show" in the palette.
    
    Phase 1 — drafting core
    - features/messaging/: trigger catalog, lifecycle due-message engine and
      deterministic draft renderers, mirrored into
      functions/src/communications/lifecycle-core.ts per the repo's
      separate-package convention.
    - aiMessageDraftCommand: single entry point for AI-prepared client
      messages. Every draft lands in the AI review queue as
      review_required; recipients are set deterministically, never by the
      model. Lifecycle triggers render with no model call or quota spend.
    - lifecycleMessageScheduler (daily 13:00 UTC), dispatchDraft
      communications command, DraftCard subject/body editor in the queue,
      and per-crew-member retainers across schema, command, portal API and
      the package form.
    
    Phase 2 — differentiators
    - aiTimingRulesCommand learns timing rules from a pasted past schedule;
      proposals carry rationale and persist only through the existing
      deterministic saveTimingRule on owner approval.
    - coiChaseScheduler (daily 14:00 UTC) re-queues outstanding COI requests
      weekly, capped at 3 chases, idempotent per chase, audited.
    - Crew cascade acceptance queues add_crew_calendar_invite; delivery
      recording chains a delivery-email draft into the review queue.
    
    Phase 3 — intelligence
    - lifecycleSettingsCommand (owner-only, audited) + LifecyclePackPanel:
      per-message On/Off and review-vs-automatic. Auto-send is restricted to
      deterministic template-rendered messages that have a recipient and
      zero missing facts; AI-personalized drafts always require review.
    - Copilot answers end with prepared-action chips that create queue
      drafts — Copilot still never sends. Dashboard leads with "Drafts
      waiting for approval".
    
    Trust boundary: the auto-send path writes only aiActions, emailJobs,
    actionReceipts and productEvents — no payment, signature or readiness
    fields — and lifecycle-core.ts performs no Firestore writes at all.
    
    Verified: typecheck clean, lint 0 errors, 202/202 unit tests passing,
    functions build clean.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

